  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funding to activities aimed at improving the resilience of tea production to climate change and variability - Luxmi project - ROS (climate finance component 30%)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Funding to activities aimed at improving the resilience of tea production to climate change and variability - Luxmi project - ROS (climate finance component 30%) is a component of Sustainable Inclusive Livelihoods through Tea Production in Rwanda reported by FCDO with a funding type of 111 - Not for profit organisation and a budget of &#xA3;618,937. It works in the following sector(s): Agricultural development, Agricultural land resources.</narrative>
  </description>
